# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every platform, whatever
# core.autocrlf says; git still decides which files are binary. Several gates of
# `./gradlew check` compare a committed file with freshly generated text character
# for character — the file maps, the browser editor's constants, the bundled
# documents, the cookbook, the external-automation and settings-help references,
# the golden run traces — and the store-listing gates count every character Play
# receives. A CRLF checkout fails all of them: with core.autocrlf=true the English
# full description reads as 4024 characters against Play's limit of 4000.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows scripts keep Windows line endings.
*.bat text eol=crlf
